  "body": "Stacked on #4242. This PR has the base `main` (a fork branch cannot be a base), but it contains the commits of #4242. Merge #4242 first. Then this PR takes `git merge origin/main`, a new gate, and shows only its own commits. Do not merge this PR before #4242: a merge would also land #4242.\n\n## What changed\n\nThis is the first slice of #4095. The issue stays open for the rest.\n\n- New: one HEIDENHAIN dialect resolver in the post crate, `camcraft_post::post::heidenhain_dialect` (table in `heidenhain_profiles.rs`). It maps `controller.identity` (model, NC software, installed options) to a profile and a flag set. The post engine gives the result to each script as `machine.heidenhainDialect`: the flags, or `{ \"error\": \"<why>\" }`.\n- The resolver parses the canonical values of `docs/research/heidenhain/dialects.md` section 1. It refuses by name an unknown model, a paraxial model (TNC 124/128), a malformed NC software identifier, release `00`, an unnamed release, a variant outside its family, and a malformed option number.\n- DIN/ISO post (`assets/posts/heidenhain.cps`):\n  - The resolver replaces the #4172 table (`drillLevel()` now reads `drillC200`).\n  - A stated control that the resolver refuses, or that has no DIN/ISO programs (`languageIso`), is refused by name at the program start.\n  - `G247 Q339=n` is refused by name where cycle 247 is not a preset-table row (`cycle247`).\n  - A machine with no controller identity keeps the output of today.\n- Klartext post (`assets/posts/heidenhain-klartext.cps`):\n  - The resolver replaces the fixed language check. A profile that does not confirm M140, cycle 247 as a preset-table row and M137 is refused by name. Coordinates use the profile's `decimals`.\n  - The manual quill procedure stays verified for iTNC 530 NC 340490-03 only (#4114). The refusal now names the resolved profile.\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/4095-heidenhain-dialect-resolver.md`. It lists each flag with its research source.\n\n## Flags wired, with sources\n\n| Flag | Post use | Source (`docs/research/heidenhain/differences.md`) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `languageIso` | DIN/ISO: refuse when not `yes` | B2 \"DIN/ISO programs\" |\n| `decimals` | Klartext: coordinate rounding; DIN/ISO: writes 3, refuses fewer | B2 \"Coordinate decimals\" |\n| `drillC200` | DIN/ISO: G200 with or without Q395; `base` refused | B2 \"Cycle 200 Q list\", B3 |\n| `cycle247` | DIN/ISO: G247 only for `presetTable`; Klartext: refuse otherwise | B2 \"Cycle 247 DATUM SETTING\" |\n| `m140`, `m136m137` | Klartext: refuse when not `yes` | B2 \"M140\"; section B (iTNC 530 340 420, TNC 410) |\n| `dwell` | no branch: DIN/ISO always writes `G04 F` (#4093); pinned on a `functionDwell` control | B2 \"Cycle 9\", \"FUNCTION DWELL\" |\n| `toolCallByName`, `toolNameMax` | resolved and table-tested; no branch, both posts write the tool number form | B2 \"Tool name in quotes\", \"Name length\" |\n\n## Golden output\n\n- No golden file changes. The Fehlmann Picomax 55 (iTNC 530, NC 340490-03) resolves to `itnc-49x`, which gives the output of today for both posts.\n- Behaviour changes only for identities that no shipped machine file states. The decision file lists them (for example TNC 320 340 551-01 to -03 are now refused by the DIN/ISO post, and iTNC 530 340 420 now posts G200 at the Q211 level).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-post` lib, `post::heidenhain_dialect::tests` (13 tests): each version boundary of each wired flag on both sides, the Picomax profile, refusals of unknown and paraxial models, malformed identifiers, unnamed releases, option numbers, the script value.\n- `heidenhain_cycles::levels`: `controls_before_the_q395_level_write_g200_without_q395`, `controls_from_the_q395_level_keep_q395`, `an_unknown_control_or_version_is_refused_by_name`, `a_control_without_din_iso_programs_is_refused_by_name`, `a_cycle_200_without_q211_is_refused_by_name`, `a_malformed_or_unsupported_nc_identifier_is_refused_by_name`, `picomax_340490_03_writes_g200_without_q395_and_the_peck_chain`.\n- `heidenhain_cycles::presets`: `a_preset_table_control_selects_the_row`, `g247_is_refused_where_cycle_247_is_not_a_preset_row`.\n- `heidenhain_block_form`: the dwell test now pins `G04 F` on TNC 426 280 472 and TNC 410 (3 decimals), and a refusal of a spaced NC string.\n- `script_heidenhain_klartext::dialect_tests`: `the_dialect_resolver_decides_the_klartext_profile`, `the_picomax_profile_writes_four_decimals`.\n\n## Gate results (head f7c90c39f2939ea1e9f7bb874e28aa130f06e036)\n\nAll steps ran on the Mac. The diff base is the #4242 branch (`8bdabe9bc`), because this PR is stacked.\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post --lib heidenhain_dialect`: 13 passed.\n- `camcraft-post` integration binaries `heidenhain_cycles` (21), `heidenhain_block_form` (6), `script_heidenhain_klartext` (29), `script_heidenhain` (16), `machine_controller` (5), `heidenhain_arc_centre` (2): all passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base qsmits/issue/4224-heidenhain-peck-chain`: 315 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (25.0 min). This includes `post lib`, `app:klartext_builtin`, `app:conformance`, `app:drill_rplane` and the other app suites that the gate maps to the post engine.\n- Example catalog suites: `example_catalog` ok, `example_catalog_adaptive` ok, `example_catalog_edge_work` ok (inside the quick gate).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed (11.8 min).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real control loaded the programs. The flags come from the research notes only.\n- No heavy step (P6).\n\n## Left for later slices of #4095\n\n- Klartext: serve other iTNC 530 releases after the manual procedure is verified for them; `TOOL CALL \"NAME\"` (`toolCallByName`, `toolNameMax`); the dwell form (`dwell`); drilling cycles with `drill.c205`; M91/M92 retract where `m140` is no.\n- Flags not in this slice: `drill.c205`, `oldCycles`, `tilt`, `tcpm.kt`/`tcpm.iso`, `planeAxial`, `planeSym`, `feedFzFu`, `arcs.spatial`, `arcs.helixLin`, `q.*`, `programName`, `tolerance` (G62).\n- Option gating from `installed_options` (tilting option 8/1, TCPM option 9/2, TNC 620 option 19 for cycles 201-205/208/209). The options are parsed now, but no flag reads them.\n- `m136m137` for the TNC 320/620/640 and TNC7: the research does not settle it (unknown).\n\nChangelog: The HEIDENHAIN DIN/ISO and Klartext posts read one dialect table for the stated control and NC software. A control or version that the table does not know, or that has no DIN/ISO programs, is refused by name. G247 is refused where cycle 247 does not select a preset-table row.\n\nEffort: max\n\nRefs #4095\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
